Of course they can.

255
00:10:29,439 --> 00:10:33,400
George! I'm going to have
new red shoes!

256
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:34,839
Oink. Oink.

257
00:10:34,839 --> 00:10:36,839
[♪♪♪]

258
00:10:36,839 --> 00:10:40,760
NARRATOR:
Mummy Pig and Peppa
are at Miss Rabbit's shoe shop.

259
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:41,959
Hello,
Miss Rabbit.

260
00:10:41,959 --> 00:10:43,640
Hello,
Mummy Pig.

261
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:46,240
Oink. We would like to buy some
new shoes for Peppa, please.

262
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:47,839
Oink. Red shoes.

263
00:10:47,839 --> 00:10:50,680
Oh, I'm sure we can find you
some lovely new shoes, Peppa.

264
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:53,079
Red ones. Oink. Please.

265
00:10:53,079 --> 00:10:55,839
Of course. Red ones.

266
00:10:55,839 --> 00:10:57,600
Wow!

267
00:10:57,600 --> 00:11:00,560
[♪♪♪]

268
00:11:00,560 --> 00:11:02,839
Oink. Oink. New red shoes!

269
00:11:02,839 --> 00:11:05,319
[LAUGHS]

270
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:10,079
NARRATOR:
George and Daddy Pig
are playing draughts.

271
00:11:10,079 --> 00:11:13,319
Oink, oink.
Oh, well done, George.

272
00:11:13,319 --> 00:11:15,640
Daddy! Daddy!
Ha-ha-ha. Oink.

273
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:17,280
Look at
my new shoes!

274
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:18,760
They're red!

275
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:20,880
I say! They are red.

276
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:23,520
Oink. Mummy, do you
like my new shoes?

277
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:26,719
Yes, Peppa they make
you look very smart.

278
00:11:26,719 --> 00:11:29,839
Oink. George.
Do you like my new shoes?

279
00:11:30,439 --> 00:11:31,880
Oink. Oink.

280
00:11:31,880 --> 00:11:34,280
NARRATOR:
Everyone likes
Peppa's new shoes.

281
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:36,719
I like my new shoes
so much

282
00:11:36,719 --> 00:11:39,600
I don't want
to ever take them off.

283
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:41,160
[ALL LAUGH]

284
00:11:41,160 --> 00:11:42,360
[♪♪♪]

285
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:44,160
NARRATOR:
It is bath time.

286
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:47,719
Peppa wants to keep her new
shoes on, even for her bath.

287
00:11:47,719 --> 00:11:49,480
[LAUGHS]

288
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:52,600
NARRATOR:
Peppa is in her pajamas.

289
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:55,120
She still has her new shoes on.

290
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:57,480
[LAUGHS]

291
00:11:57,480 --> 00:12:00,760
NARRATOR:
Peppa even wants to wear
her new shoes in bed!

292
00:12:00,760 --> 00:12:03,839
Peppa, are you sure you don't
want to take your shoes off?

293
00:12:03,839 --> 00:12:07,120
I don't want to ever take
my new shoes off, Mummy.

294
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:10,280
Ha. Very well.
Goodnight, Peppa and George.

295
00:12:10,280 --> 00:12:12,640
[LAUGHS AND OINKS]

296
00:12:12,640 --> 00:12:15,360
Ha-ha-ha. Goodnight,
Mummy. Oink.

297
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:16,920
Goodnight, Daddy.

298
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:19,680
Oink. Goodnight,
my little piggies.

299
00:12:21,280 --> 00:12:23,839
[RAIN POURING]

300
00:12:23,839 --> 00:12:28,360
NARRATOR:
It has been raining all night,
and now the garden is very wet.

301
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:30,280
Mummy Pig is wearing her boots.

302
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:32,040
Daddy Pig is
wearing his boots.

303
00:12:32,040 --> 00:12:33,400
George is wearing his boots.

304
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:37,360
Peppa is still wearing
her new red shoes.

305
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:39,000
[LAUGHS AND OINKS]

306
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:41,400
NARRATOR:
George is going to play
in the wet grass.

307
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:43,439
[LAUGHING]

308
00:12:43,439 --> 00:12:44,880
NARRATOR:
Oh, dear.

309
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:46,480
Peppa loves playing
in the wet grass,

310
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:49,520
but she doesn't want get
her new shoes wet.

311
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:52,599
I can't play
in the wet grass, George.

312
00:12:52,599 --> 00:12:54,319
Oh. Oink. Oink.

313
00:12:54,319 --> 00:12:56,040
[♪♪♪]

314
00:12:56,040 --> 00:12:58,480
NARRATOR:
George loves jumping
in muddy puddles.

315
00:12:58,480 --> 00:13:00,160
Oink. Oink.

316
00:13:00,160 --> 00:13:01,880
NARRATOR:
Peppa loves jumping in puddles,

317
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:04,240
but she doesn't want
to get her new shoes muddy.

318
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:06,240
Oh.

319
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:09,439
NARRATOR:
Mummy and Daddy love jumping up
and down in in muddy puddles.

320
00:13:09,439 --> 00:13:12,400
Everyone likes jumping
in muddy puddles.

321
00:13:12,400 --> 00:13:13,480
Oink.

322
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:14,800
[♪♪♪]

323
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:16,360
NARRATOR: 
Where is Peppa going?

324
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:17,640
Oink, oink.

325
00:13:18,599 --> 00:13:19,800
[LAUGHS]

326
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:23,160
NARRATOR:
Peppa is putting on her boots.

327
00:13:23,160 --> 00:13:24,360
[LAUGHING]

328
00:13:24,360 --> 00:13:26,120
Oink, oink.

329
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:29,319
[CONTINUES LAUGHING]

330
00:13:29,319 --> 00:13:30,520
Oink.

331
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:31,839
[ALL LAUGHING]

332
00:13:31,839 --> 00:13:33,160
Whee!

333
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:39,800
If you jump in muddy puddles,
you must wear your boots.

334
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:41,959
[ALL LAUGHING]

335
00:13:48,760 --> 00:13:51,680
[♪♪♪]

336
00:13:51,680 --> 00:13:54,400
[PEPPA READS ONSCREEN TEXT]

337
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:56,760
NARRATOR:
Today is day
of the school fete.

338
00:13:56,760 --> 00:13:59,199
Peppa loves coming to the fete.
[LAUGHING]

339
00:13:59,199 --> 00:14:02,360
NARRATOR:
Here are Peppa's friends,
Candy Cat, Suzy Sheep,

340
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:05,240
Danny Dog, Rebecca Rabbit
and Pedro Pony.

341
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:07,040
Hello, everyone. Oink.

342
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:09,760
ALL [GRUNTING]:
Hello, Peppa.

343
00:14:09,760 --> 00:14:11,920
I love the school fete.

344
00:14:11,920 --> 00:14:13,319
Me, too. Oink.

345
00:14:13,319 --> 00:14:14,560
What do you like best?

346
00:14:14,560 --> 00:14:17,520
Bleat. The face
painting.

347
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:20,479
Whinny.
I like the balloons.

348
00:14:20,479 --> 00:14:24,400
Woof, woof. I like
the bouncy castle the best.

349
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:26,839
I like everything. Oink.

350
00:14:26,839 --> 00:14:29,880
Ho, ho. A very good
choice, Peppa.

351
00:14:29,880 --> 00:14:32,120
Woof. See you
later, Peppa.

352
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:34,000
Oink. See you later.

353
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:36,680
George, what do you like best?

354
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:39,760
Dine-saw. Grrr.

355
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:43,719
Oh dear, there aren't any
dinosaurs at the fete, George.

356
00:14:43,719 --> 00:14:46,240
Maybe we can get
you a dinosaur balloon.

357
00:14:46,240 --> 00:14:49,560
Are you sure they have dinosaur
balloons, Daddy Pig?

358
00:14:49,560 --> 00:14:51,160
I'm certain of it.

359
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:52,479
Oink.

360
00:14:52,479 --> 00:14:54,760
Can George and I get
our faces painted first?

361
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:55,920
Of course.

362
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:57,719
[PEPPA &amp; GEORGE LAUGH]

363
00:14:57,719 --> 00:15:01,000
NARRATOR:
Miss Rabbit has painted
Peppa's friends as tigers.

364
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,360
There you are, Suzy.

365
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:04,400
Now you look
like a tiger.

366
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:07,360
Thank you, Miss Rabbit. Bleat.

367
00:15:07,360 --> 00:15:09,439
[PEPPA &amp; GEORGE LAUGH]

368
00:15:09,439 --> 00:15:12,400
Wow! I like
your face, Suzy.

369
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:14,199
Are you a pussycat?

370
00:15:14,199 --> 00:15:17,319
No! I'm a tiger!
Bleat.

371
00:15:17,319 --> 00:15:19,640
Peppa, would you like
your face painted?

372
00:15:19,640 --> 00:15:23,719
Yes, please.
Can I be...an elephant?

373
00:15:23,719 --> 00:15:26,800
Oh dear, I don't know
how to do elephants.

374
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:28,160
I can do tigers.

375
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:29,479
[ALL LAUGH]

376
00:15:29,479 --> 00:15:32,400
Yes, a tiger please.

377
00:15:32,400 --> 00:15:35,280
There you are Peppa,
now you're a tiger.

378
00:15:35,280 --> 00:15:37,760
Ha-ha-ha. I'm a tiger. Oink.

379
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:40,079
George, what would
you like to be?

380
00:15:40,079 --> 00:15:42,760
Dine-saw. Grrr.

381
00:15:42,760 --> 00:15:44,199
A dinosaur?

382
00:15:44,199 --> 00:15:46,520
Uh, how about
a tiger instead?

383
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:48,400
I'm good at tigers.

384
00:15:48,400 --> 00:15:49,760
Oink. Oink.

385
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:52,079
Ha-ha-ha.
I'm a tiger. Oink.

386
00:15:52,079 --> 00:15:53,479
So am I.
Woof. Woof.

387
00:15:53,479 --> 00:15:56,520
Meow. Tigers don't
say, "Woof, woof."

388
00:15:56,520 --> 00:15:58,079
How do you know?

389
00:15:58,079 --> 00:16:00,439
Because tigers are big cats.

390
00:16:00,439 --> 00:16:02,560
Meow. And I'm a cat.

391
00:16:02,560 --> 00:16:06,240
Candy, please can you teach us
how to be tigers?

392
00:16:06,240 --> 00:16:07,719
Okay.

393
00:16:07,719 --> 00:16:12,719
Tigers creep very, very slowly
and then, they jump.

394
00:16:12,719 --> 00:16:14,800
Grrr.
[ALL SCREAM]

395
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:16,160
[ALL LAUGH]

396
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:18,000
ALL:
Grrr.

397
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:21,000
Tigers like to lick
themselves clean.

398
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,439
[SLURPS]

399
00:16:23,439 --> 00:16:27,160
But, best of all, when tigers
are happy, they purr.

400
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:28,439
[PURRS]

401
00:16:28,439 --> 00:16:31,400
[ALL PURR]

402
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:32,719
Hello, children.

403
00:16:32,719 --> 00:16:34,400
Oh. My goodness.

404
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:36,120
You're all tigers.

405
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:39,319
And I'm teaching them
to be proper tigers.

406
00:16:39,319 --> 00:16:40,640
Grrr.

407
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:41,880
[LAUGHS]

408
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:43,680
What do you little tigers
want to do next?

409
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:45,520
Oink. Dine-saw.

410
00:16:45,520 --> 00:16:49,079
That's right. We have to find
George a dinosaur balloon.

411
00:16:49,079 --> 00:16:50,719
[LAUGHS]

412
00:16:50,719 --> 00:16:52,319
Let's get
you all balloons.

413
00:16:52,319 --> 00:16:53,959
ALL:
Hooray!

414
00:16:53,959 --> 00:16:56,280
[ALL LAUGHING]

415
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:57,400
Hello, Madame Gazelle.

416
00:16:57,400 --> 00:16:59,040
We'd like
some balloons, please.

417
00:16:59,040 --> 00:17:00,199
Certainly.

418
00:17:00,199 --> 00:17:02,359
I've got lots
of different ones.

419
00:17:02,359 --> 00:17:04,800
Can I have an elephant
balloon, please?

420
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:06,720
Here you are, Peppa.

421
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:08,839
Can I have a kangaroo?

422
00:17:08,839 --> 00:17:10,440
A lion, please.

423
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:11,839
A monkey, please.

424
00:17:11,839 --> 00:17:13,480
A parrot, please.

425
00:17:13,480 --> 00:17:15,720
Ho, ho. Yes, I've
got all those.

426
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:16,879
[ALL LAUGH]

427
00:17:16,879 --> 00:17:18,560
Most important
of all,

428
00:17:18,560 --> 00:17:21,800
we need a dinosaur
balloon for George.

429
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:26,560
Oh dear, I do not seem to have
any dinosaur balloons.

430
00:17:26,560 --> 00:17:29,080
Oh.

431
00:17:29,080 --> 00:17:31,280
[CRYING]

432
00:17:31,280 --> 00:17:34,720
Don't worry, George. I've got
an idea.

433
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:37,919
Could we have two of the long
balloons, please?

434
00:17:37,919 --> 00:17:39,720
Watch this,
everybody.

435
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:41,520
[♪♪♪]

436
00:17:41,520 --> 00:17:45,200
NARRATOR:
What is Daddy Pig
doing with the balloons?

437
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:48,360
There. Can anyone
guess what it is?

438
00:17:48,360 --> 00:17:50,560
Is it a kangaroo?

439
00:17:50,560 --> 00:17:53,080
Ho, ho. No, it's a--

440
00:17:53,080 --> 00:17:54,360
Dine-saw.

441
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:56,399
DADDY:
That's right. A dinosaur.

442
00:17:56,399 --> 00:17:59,480
NARRATOR:
Daddy Pig has made
a balloon dinosaur.

443
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:02,520
Grrr. Dine-saw.

444
00:18:02,520 --> 00:18:04,639
Oink.
Now the bouncy castle!

445
00:18:04,639 --> 00:18:06,560
[KIDS LAUGHING]

446
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:11,680
NARRATOR:
Peppa loves bouncing
on the bouncy castle.

447
00:18:11,680 --> 00:18:15,000
Everyone loves bouncing
on the bouncy castle.

448
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:17,639
This is the best school
fete, ever.

449
00:18:17,639 --> 00:18:18,919
[ALL LAUGHING]

450
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:21,639
[♪♪♪]

451
00:18:21,639 --> 00:18:24,760
♪ Peppa Pig
Oink ♪

452
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:27,000
[PEPPA LAUGHS AND OINKS]

453
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:29,159
♪ Peppa Pig
Oink ♪

454
00:18:29,159 --> 00:18:31,120
[MORE LAUGHING AND OINKING]

455
00:18:31,120 --> 00:18:33,800
♪ Peppa Pig
Oink ♪

